&lt;p&gt;Next.js 15 is the biggest update since the App Router. Turbopack is now the default bundler. Partial Prerendering combines static and dynamic content. Server Actions are stable. The framework is faster, simpler, and more production-ready than ever.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What's New in Next.js 15
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Turbopack&lt;/strong&gt; — default dev server bundler, 10x faster than webpack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Partial Prerendering (PPR)&lt;/strong&gt; — static shell + dynamic holes, one request&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Server Actions stable&lt;/strong&gt; — form mutations without API routes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Improved caching&lt;/strong&gt; — fetch requests no longer cached by default&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;React 19&lt;/strong&gt; — use() hook, async components, improved Suspense&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

